TSA-fortran v0.5.0

This is a source translation of computational routines from the R package TSA
version 1.3.1, by Kung-Sik Chan and Brian Ripley. TSA is distributed under
GPL (>= 2). The complete original package used for this translation is retained
verbatim under upstream/TSA-1.3.1.

TSA's arima/arimax R source states that it is based on R's stats::arima code and
contains the R Core Team GPL notice. Those original files are preserved verbatim
under upstream/TSA-1.3.1/R/arima.R and upstream/TSA-1.3.1/R/arimax.R.

The user-supplied modern Fortran translations of leaps, locfit, mgcv, and tseries
are retained under vendor/ with their original licenses and attribution files.
The compiled TSA source reuses the required leaps and tseries modules under
src/dependencies/ so that this FPM package builds standalone. Those files are
copied without changing their upstream translation licenses.

TSA imports locfit and mgcv only in lagplot(), a graphical routine. Because this
translation intentionally omits plotting code, locfit and mgcv are preserved in
vendor/ for provenance but are not compiled into the library.

The combined bundle may be redistributed under GPL version 2 or GPL version 3;
see LICENSE, LICENSE-GPL-2, LICENSE-GPL-3, and component license files.
No warranty is provided.

Versions 0.3.0 through 0.5.0 additionally translate computational behavior
delegated by TSA to R's stats package, notably diffuse ARIMA state-space
likelihood, the default Gardner/AS154 covariance initializer, BFGS/Hessian
behavior, `spec.pgram`, `spec.ar`, and compact spectral-kernel calculations. R
source used as a parity reference is GPL-2-or-later; no additional R source file
is vendored beyond the copies already present in upstream TSA.
